---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
import boards from "../data/boards.json";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Site title="Hardware">
  <section class="wrap page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">KNOW WHAT IS IN YOUR HAND</p>
    <h1>
      Small boards.
      <br />
      Different possibilities.
    </h1>
    <p class="intro">The small computer at the heart of your project.</p>
    <p>
      A microcontroller board runs a program and talks to lights or sensors
      through its connection pins. Add LEDs, wiring, power and LightVM firmware
      to turn it into a lighting controller. These are standard development
      boards you can buy separately, rather than a special KajLights kit.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section narrow prose" id="find-a-board">
    <h2>Where do I find one?</h2>
    <p>
      For a first lighting project, the <strong>Raspberry Pi Pico 2 W</strong>{" "}
      is the example used in our{" "}
      <a href={`${base}build/`}>parts and build guide</a>. Start at{" "}
      <a href="https://www.raspberrypi.com/products/raspberry-pi-pico-2/">
        Raspberry Pi’s product page and retailer finder
      </a>
      , select <strong>Pico 2 W</strong>, and choose your country. Look for a
      version with headers already soldered on if you want to use jumper wires.
      A Pico is a microcontroller board, not a Raspberry Pi desktop computer;
      this project does not need an SD card, keyboard or monitor for the board.
    </p>
    <p>
      Already have a board? Compare the printed name with the models below. For
      the smaller XIAO boards, use Seeed’s official model guides:{" "}
      <a href="https://wiki.seeedstudio.com/XIAO_ESP32C3_Getting_Started/">
        ESP32-C3
      </a>
      ,{" "}
      <a href="https://wiki.seeedstudio.com/xiao_esp32s3_getting_started/">
        ESP32-S3
      </a>{" "}
      and{" "}
      <a href="https://wiki.seeedstudio.com/xiao_esp32c6_getting_started/">
        ESP32-C6
      </a>
      . Those guides include pin diagrams and purchase links. A generic “ESP32”
      listing is not enough to identify a compatible board.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Before buying:</strong> check the{" "}
      <a href={`${base}releases/`}>release catalogue</a> for your exact model.
      These are development targets; a listing here does not mean a tested
      public installer is available. During early testing, setting up hardware
      may require building firmware from source. You can try the{" "}
      <a href="https://kajlights.github.io/lightvm/">browser playground</a>{" "}
      without buying anything.
    </p>
    <h2>Identify your model</h2>
    <p>
      Use the printed model to identify your board. Flash sizes below describe
      the standard board configuration; the ESP installer measures physical
      flash before writing.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap board-grid" aria-label="Board models">
    {boards.map((board) => (
      <article class="board-card" id={board.id}>
        <span class="board-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <i></i>
          <b>{board.id.startsWith("pico") ? "RP" : "X"}</b>
          <i></i>
        </span>
        <p class="eyebrow">
          {board.chip} · {board.flash_bytes / 1048576} MiB NOMINAL FLASH
        </p>
        <h2>{board.name}</h2>
        <p>{board.hint}</p>
        <p class="muted">
          {board.method === "uf2"
            ? `Hold BOOTSEL while connecting. Copy the selected UF2 to the ${board.drive} drive.`
            : "Choose its USB port in the workspace. Chip, revision and flash must match before installation."}
        </p>
        <a
          class="text-link"
          href={`${base}studio/#/firmware?board=${board.id}`}
        >
          Find firmware →
        </a>
      </article>
    ))}
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section narrow prose">
    <h2>Working with sound</h2>
    <p>
      kaj-fi is a separate analyser project for the XIAO ESP32-S3 Sense
      microphone and synthetic test signals. Existing devices can use the shared
      workspace for identity and nicknames. Public firmware distribution has not
      yet been enabled.
    </p>
  </section>
</Site>
